kind: profile
question: how many target tokens does a GLM MTP verification keep on one and two DGX Sparks?
term: kept target positions divided by completed verification windows, with lossless greedy IDs;
  accompanying decode times compare MTP off and on in the same build and sitting
unit: tokens/verify
predict: 1..2
condition: GLM-5.3-Flash UD-Q4_K_XL, short and 4096-token prompts, one request, graph target;
  two is the GLM verification window's row capacity, not a measured acceptance claim; alternate off/on twice
  on one Spark and two Sparks, with the same prompt, context and target placement in each pair;
  record current-main and head TP2 attempts in the same lease, including named refusals;
  builds and copies finish before the lease, no unrelated CUDA or test process, load average
  below one for 30 seconds, default clock policy; clock, power, temperature, memory and page-cache
  witnesses bracket the sitting, with plain-read and link-byte/latency ceilings in that sitting
decide-in: record the acceptance row and compare the accompanying off/on decode time without claiming a main speedup
decide-below: diagnose a verification that kept no target token before accepting its rate
decide-above: diagnose a counter exceeding the verification window's two-row capacity before publishing the row
